1
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,239
You can't see Kang Qingsong.

2
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:44,200
Why can't I see him?

3
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,719
It's a special case requiring special clearance.

4
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,560
We made an appointment

5
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,760
to see him at this time.

6
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,040
Why are you restricting

7
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,359
a lawyer from seeing their client?

8
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,519
Your approval process isn't complete yet.

9
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,599
This is really urgent.

10
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,319
Zhou Hao.

11
00:01:57,319 --> 00:01:57,799
I'm telling you,

12
00:01:57,799 --> 00:01:58,840
if I don't see him in person today,

13
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,159
I'm not leaving, got it?

14
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:01,120
Calm down.

15
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,680
Come on, let's step outside first.

16
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,599
Let's go.

17
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:31,960
Ding Ning, you're back

18
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,919
I saved some food for you

19
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:35,599
I already had takeout

20
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,280
Alright, good

21
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,080
You should come back for a home-cooked meal when you can

22
00:02:42,199 --> 00:02:44,000
Eating out all the time...

23
00:02:44,319 --> 00:02:46,759
It's not very hygienic or nutritious

24
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,280
What's wrong?

25
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,439
You look so tired

26
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,080
How is your case going?

27
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,560
The jurisdictional objection was overruled

28
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,400
At least I don't have to go back to Rongshan

29
00:02:59,080 --> 00:02:59,719
But...

30
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,639
Never mind, let's not talk about it

31
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,240
It's giving me a headache

32
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,319
How is Awu today? Still making a fuss?

33
00:03:06,319 --> 00:03:07,680
He sure is

34
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,639
Of course he is

35
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,000
It's just that...

36
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,280
He speaks his local dialect

37
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,840
I... I can't understand him

38
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,240
I don't know what he wants

39
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,240
I'm thinking of sending him to school in a few days

40
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,560
To learn some Mandarin

41
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:22,080
Actually, if you want to talk about your case

42
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,680
I don't mind listening

43
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,479
Weird. Really weird.

44
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,360
What's going on?

45
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,840
First, Lao Kang's case is moving very fast.

46
00:03:38,199 --> 00:03:39,960
Second, from the time I took it over until now,

47
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,240
it's been about half a month, right?

48
00:03:41,879 --> 00:03:43,159
We haven't had any way

49
00:03:43,159 --> 00:03:44,639
to see Lao Kang at the detention center.

50
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,599
But seeing your client

51
00:03:50,599 --> 00:03:52,199
is your basic right.

52
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:54,360
How could they not let you see him?

53
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:54,960
Exactly.

54
00:03:55,879 --> 00:03:56,840
They said something like...

55
00:03:58,439 --> 00:03:59,520
Lao Kang's case

56
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,280
requires a certificate from the task force.

57
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:05,919
Didn't you say Lao Kang has a gun?

58
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:08,439
Could he really be in a crime syndicate?

59
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,840
That's the third weird point.

60
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:13,240
They arrested him based on a single confession.

61
00:04:14,159 --> 00:04:15,560
We don't even know if it's true.

62
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:17,839
While they were investigating if a gang was involved

63
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:19,279
in some criminal activity,

64
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,800
a low-level thug suddenly popped up and said

65
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,399
he took part in an armed robbery four years ago,

66
00:04:24,399 --> 00:04:26,000
and Lao Kang was one of his accomplices.

67
00:04:26,439 --> 00:04:28,199
Doesn't that confirm Lao Kang

68
00:04:28,199 --> 00:04:29,480
was an accessory in this case?

69
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,399
Let me finish.

70
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:31,759
Let's leave aside the fact

71
00:04:31,759 --> 00:04:32,879
that this thug was being investigated

72
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,519
clearly for bribery.

73
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:36,759
But why would he come forward for no reason

74
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:39,040
and confess to an armed robbery from four years ago?

75
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:42,759
Who would want to add to their own charges for nothing?

76
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,839
And by saying that,

77
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:45,240
he'll have to serve a few more years in prison.

78
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:47,000
True.

79
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,959
It is pretty unusual.

80
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,360
Yeah.

81
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,279
He also said

82
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:53,639
the day before his armed robbery,

83
00:04:53,759 --> 00:04:55,519
he and two accomplices, including Lao Kang,

84
00:04:55,519 --> 00:04:57,360
robbed a phone store with hunting rifles.

85
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,480
And they never contacted each other after that.

86
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,759
Isn't that strange?

87
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:02,959
What's strange about it?

88
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:06,759
Listen to me.

89
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:09,360
First of all, they might not be

90
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,279
a fixed criminal crew.

91
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:14,160
They might have just decided to pull a job on a whim.

92
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,079
After splitting the loot,

93
00:05:15,079 --> 00:05:16,000
never seeing each other again

94
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
isn't that strange.

95
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,800
Plus, Lao Kang is a hunter.

96
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,199
He has an unregistered gun.

97
00:05:22,279 --> 00:05:24,279
Now someone has come forward to testify.

98
00:05:24,399 --> 00:05:27,040
Doesn't that mean they have witness and material evidence?

99
00:05:27,279 --> 00:05:27,920
Therefore,

100
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:31,600
the procuratorate has enough evidence to review and prosecute.

101
00:05:31,639 --> 00:05:32,199
No.

102
00:05:32,199 --> 00:05:34,079
I'm talking about two different things right now.

103
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,279
Lao Kang having an illegal gun is one thing,

104
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:39,360
and whether he actually committed armed robbery

105
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,480
is another.

106
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,360
Of course, of course.

107
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,639
You can't say that because he has an illegal gun,

108
00:05:42,639 --> 00:05:44,680
he definitely used it to commit crimes, right?

109
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,160
And then punish him to the fullest extent.

110
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,519
Besides, all the hunters over there have guns.

111
00:05:48,519 --> 00:05:49,759
They're just unregistered.

112
00:05:49,879 --> 00:05:51,680
Evidence, evidence, evidence.

113
00:05:52,079 --> 00:05:56,480
The procuratorate now has witnesses and physical evidence.

114
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,000
Unless you...

115
00:05:58,959 --> 00:06:01,399
you can find an alibi for Lao Kang.

116
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:05,279
That's my biggest headache right now.

117
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,519
Plus, it's deep in the mountains.

118
00:06:07,519 --> 00:06:08,959
Not everyone has a cell phone.

119
00:06:09,079 --> 00:06:09,920
There's no time.

120
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,279
Right, there's no time.

121
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:17,720
I'm going out for a bit.

122
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:19,879
What is it?

123
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,279
You just got back, where are you going?

124
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:36,759
Hey, Ding Ning.

125
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,560
I told the front desk to let you in.

126
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,000
I'll be right there.

127
00:07:31,199 --> 00:07:33,120
Ding Ning, did you find anything new?

128
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,360
Zhou Hao.

129
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:37,279
The problem lies in how the bribe money was withdrawn.

130
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,560
According to the confession,

131
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,399
the thug said that on the morning of July 9th,

132
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,519
he went to four banks

133
00:07:42,519 --> 00:07:44,079
and an ATM to withdraw cash.

134
00:07:45,319 --> 00:07:46,360
After getting the money,

135
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,000
he dropped it off at his place.

136
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,800
Only then did he meet up with Lao Kang.

137
00:07:49,959 --> 00:07:52,240
Then, the three of them robbed the phone store.

138
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:52,839
Right?

139
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:53,759
Yes, exactly.

140
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,199
The crime occurred at 11:10 a.m.

141
00:07:56,759 --> 00:07:57,639
In other words,

142
00:07:57,839 --> 00:07:59,399
withdrawing the 500,000

143
00:07:59,399 --> 00:08:02,000
must have been completed before 11:00.

144
00:08:02,319 --> 00:08:03,319
But is that possible?

145
00:08:04,399 --> 00:08:06,319
Following the route mentioned in the confession,

146
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,920
I visited the banks he mentioned

147
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,839
and the ATM.

148
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,439
Assuming no traffic and no queues,

149
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,639
it takes at least an hour and a half.

150
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:16,360
Plus, the banks don't open until 9:00 a.m.

151
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,439
So it seems fine, right?

152
00:08:18,639 --> 00:08:19,839
But the catch is,

153
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:23,480
this street didn't look like this four years ago.

154
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,399
I used a city map from four years ago

155
00:08:27,399 --> 00:08:28,399
and tested it again.

156
00:08:28,639 --> 00:08:30,399
This time, the fastest it could be done

157
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,720
was by 1:00 p.m.

158
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,120
This means

159
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:34,399
the thug who went to withdraw the money

160
00:08:34,399 --> 00:08:35,639
couldn't possibly have had the time

161
00:08:35,639 --> 00:08:37,080
to commit an armed robbery.

162
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,960
Do you get it now, Zhou Hao?

163
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:41,200
This guy is lying.

164
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:43,200
If he went to get the money,

165
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,000
he wouldn't have had time for the robbery.

166
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,519
But the armed robbery case

167
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,679
definitely happened.

168
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,480
The traces at the crime scene,

169
00:08:49,759 --> 00:08:51,159
and the victims from back then...

170
00:08:51,159 --> 00:08:52,960
Of course the robbery happened.

171
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,519
The evidence and time of the crime

172
00:08:54,519 --> 00:08:56,080
are also set in stone.

173
00:08:56,519 --> 00:08:57,320
However,

174
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,960
they got the wrong person.

175
00:08:59,399 --> 00:09:02,120
He might not be the actual robber.

176
00:09:02,279 --> 00:09:03,080
If it wasn't him,

177
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,799
then why would he confess?

178
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,039
That's exactly what we need

179
00:09:07,039 --> 00:09:08,639
to dig into next.

180
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:10,159
But the main point is,

181
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,559
if he wasn't there,

182
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,720
then his claim that Lao Kang was involved

183
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,840
is completely unreliable.

184
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,039
We just invalidated this key evidence.

185
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,360
This is indeed a major breakthrough.

186
00:09:21,159 --> 00:09:22,320
Hold on a second, don't hang up.

187
00:09:28,399 --> 00:09:29,240
Are you still there?

188
00:09:30,039 --> 00:09:31,679
Let me continue my train of thought.

189
00:09:32,039 --> 00:09:33,960
If we want to solidify this evidence,

190
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,840
we need to promptly apply to the procuratorate.

191
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,480
Ding Ning.

192
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:38,399
Go ahead.

193
00:09:38,559 --> 00:09:39,879
Lao Kang confessed.

194
00:09:58,519 --> 00:09:59,759
Then go see Lao Kang.

195
00:10:00,279 --> 00:10:01,720
At all costs.

196
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,200
Zhao. Xu.

197
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,799
What brings you here?

198
00:10:19,799 --> 00:10:21,559
I've made a major discovery

199
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,320
about Lao Kang's case.

200
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,159
Lao Kang is innocent.

201
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:32,200
The punk who implicated him in the robbery

202
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,600
framed him.

203
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:37,200
What do you mean?

204
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,600
There's an issue with the confession.

205
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:40,600
What issue?

206
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,279
That punk is actually lying.

207
00:10:43,399 --> 00:10:44,759
He forgot that the street four years ago

208
00:10:44,759 --> 00:10:46,159
was different from how it is now.

209
00:10:46,279 --> 00:10:48,799
So if he was the one withdrawing the bribe money,

210
00:10:48,919 --> 00:10:51,039
he wouldn't have had time for the robbery at noon.

211
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,799
Really.

212
00:10:52,279 --> 00:10:53,559
I simulated it myself several times.

213
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:54,480
There really wasn't enough time.

214
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:57,440
So his confession doesn't hold up at all.

215
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,320
He implicated Lao Kang,

216
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,559
which means it's a frame-up.

217
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,960
Even though Lao Kang already pleaded guilty,

218
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,679
but...

219
00:11:06,039 --> 00:11:08,440
if I can just meet him at the detention center,

220
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,440
and summarize my findings

221
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,519
to submit to the judge...

222
00:11:11,799 --> 00:11:13,879
Did you come here specifically

223
00:11:13,879 --> 00:11:14,879
to see us about this?

224
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:15,519
Yeah.

225
00:11:15,879 --> 00:11:17,679
That must have taken you hours back and forth.

226
00:11:17,679 --> 00:11:18,840
You could have just called

227
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,919
or sent a text.

228
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,240
But this is too important.

229
00:11:22,799 --> 00:11:24,279
It's about Lao Kang's fate!

230
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,000
Right now, the detention center

231
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,879
keeps using task force approval as an excuse

232
00:11:27,879 --> 00:11:28,879
to stop me from seeing Lao Kang.

233
00:11:28,879 --> 00:11:30,200
It's not an excuse.

234
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,200
Anti-gang cases

235
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,600
all have to go through this visitation procedure.

236
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,200
If you really worry about Lao Kang's fate,

237
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,200
instead of coming to us for help,

238
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,480
you should go straight to the task force.

239
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:48,480
Okay.

240
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:50,960
Okay.

241
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,639
Then... then I'll head back.

242
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,559
Good luck with the trial.

243
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,360
Wait,

244
00:11:57,799 --> 00:11:59,600
this crucial discovery...

245
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:01,759
Did you find it yourself?

246
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:04,840
Yes.

247
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,519
I stayed up for several nights

248
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,519
going through all the case files to find it.

249
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,399
Does anyone else know?

250
00:12:16,159 --> 00:12:16,879
No.

251
00:12:17,759 --> 00:12:18,799
No one else knows.

252
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,480
Good.

253
00:12:21,639 --> 00:12:22,440
How about this,

254
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,279
keep it a secret for now.

255
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,559
If you manage to meet him,

256
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,200
let me know, okay?

257
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:31,200
Okay.

258
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,200
I'll get going then.

259
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:37,440
Goodbye, Zhao.

260
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,200
Goodbye, Xu.

261
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,879
I always thought she was just a kid.

262
00:12:43,039 --> 00:12:44,159
She's a good kid, I suppose.

263
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:45,759
But she needs to learn to shut up first.

264
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,600
Awu...

265
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,440
Awu, stop playing.

266
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,519
Yang Awu!

267
00:13:20,519 --> 00:13:22,679
Yang Awu, where are you?

268
00:13:22,679 --> 00:13:23,960
Come out and take a bath.

269
00:13:26,559 --> 00:13:27,240
Seriously.

270
00:13:28,399 --> 00:13:30,200
Are you trying to tear my house apart?

271
00:13:31,399 --> 00:13:32,039
Awu!

272
00:13:33,639 --> 00:13:35,159
Come out and take a bath!

273
00:13:35,519 --> 00:13:36,399
Awu!

274
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,559
Be a good boy.

275
00:13:37,559 --> 00:13:38,559
Where are you going?

276
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:41,320
Let's go take a bath, okay?

277
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,440
I want to go home! I want to go home!

278
00:13:44,799 --> 00:13:46,399
What's wrong with being here?

279
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,360
You haven't bathed in days since you got here.

280
00:13:50,879 --> 00:13:51,919
You stink, you know that?

281
00:13:51,919 --> 00:13:53,000
No! I won't wash!

282
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,279
Be good, come here.

283
00:13:55,879 --> 00:13:57,279
Come here, come here!

284
00:13:57,279 --> 00:13:59,960
Turns out you speak Mandarin better than I do.

285
00:14:00,639 --> 00:14:02,000
What have you been pretending for?

286
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,679
What are you pretending for? Come take a bath!

287
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,360
If you keep this up, I'll...

288
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:08,360
If you don't take a bath, you'll smell.

289
00:14:08,519 --> 00:14:10,919
Bugs will bite you if you stink, you know?

290
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:11,960
Stand still! Stand still!

291
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:12,720
No! I won't wash!

292
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,679
I want to see Dad!

293
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,080
Okay, okay, okay.

294
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:22,919
Grandpa promises you.

295
00:14:23,799 --> 00:14:24,840
If you wash up clean,

296
00:14:25,279 --> 00:14:27,120
I'll take you to see Dad, okay?

297
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,440
Come on, be a good boy.

298
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:29,960
Come here, be good.

299
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,120
Dad doesn't want me.

300
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,720
He brought me here. I don't like it.

301
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,600
Okay, come here, it's fine.

302
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:41,679
There are no friends here.

303
00:14:43,919 --> 00:14:44,960
Okay, okay, okay.

304
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,679
Good, very good.

305
00:14:47,879 --> 00:14:48,519
Stand still.

306
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,759
How did this happen? Who did this?

307
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:56,039
Uncle.

308
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,360
And here?

309
00:15:01,679 --> 00:15:02,320
Auntie.

310
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,080
So Dad found out they were abusing you,

311
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,639
and brought you home, right?

312
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,559
Was Dad good to you?

313
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,960
Yes, Dad is good.

314
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,360
I eat a lot.

315
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:20,559
And Dad doesn't hit me.

316
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,080
But why doesn't he want me now?

317
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,240
No.

318
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,000
It's not that he doesn't want you.

319
00:15:31,159 --> 00:15:32,679
Everyone likes you.

320
00:15:32,679 --> 00:15:33,919
Everyone's fighting to have you.

321
00:15:33,919 --> 00:15:34,720
Do you know that?

322
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:38,879
It's just that Lao Kang has no choice.

323
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,440
He did something wrong.

324
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,120
Dad... did something wrong?

325
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,120
That's right.

326
00:15:48,799 --> 00:15:50,360
Because he did something wrong,

327
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:53,639
he won't be able to see you for a few years.

328
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,080
Don't be afraid.

329
00:15:59,919 --> 00:16:01,159
Grandpa is here with you.

330
00:16:01,759 --> 00:16:02,720
Grandpa will take care of you.

331
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:06,039
What if you do something wrong too?

332
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:15,960
Grandpa promises you,

333
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,000
Grandpa won't do anything wrong.

334
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:19,519
Be a good boy.

335
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,080
Grandpa won't do anything wrong.

336
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,879
Grandpa will always stay with Awu, okay?

337
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:38,279
I was just about to call you, Zhao Yijie.

338
00:16:38,279 --> 00:16:39,480
During the judges' orientation,

339
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,159
is the most important lesson not answering the phone?

340
00:16:41,159 --> 00:16:42,799
Yang Cheng has been calling you for three days.

341
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,559
Don't talk to me about Yang Cheng.

342
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,679
Yang Awu is being abused. He's covered in bruises.

343
00:16:46,679 --> 00:16:47,840
Did you know? Answer me!

344
00:16:48,639 --> 00:16:49,080
What?

345
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,759
Ever since this child was born,

346
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:53,159
he's never seen his father or his mother.

347
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,720
He's just been passed around.

348
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,440
He's never had a proper home.

349
00:16:57,960 --> 00:17:00,360
You just send money to his place to raise him.

350
00:17:00,639 --> 00:17:02,279
Have you ever truly cared about him?

351
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:06,839
Zhao Yijie, you used me as a tool.

352
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:08,000
I accepted it. I let it go.

353
00:17:08,119 --> 00:17:10,880
Now you're using my grandson as your tool too.

354
00:17:11,519 --> 00:17:12,799
Do you have a conscience?

355
00:17:15,079 --> 00:17:19,680
Did Yang Awu tell you who did it?

356
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,200
Lao Kang?

357
00:17:21,359 --> 00:17:22,319
Not Lao Kang.

358
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:23,640
Lao Kang treats him very well.

359
00:17:24,319 --> 00:17:25,119
It's his uncle.

360
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:30,759
Alright, I get it.

361
00:17:30,759 --> 00:17:31,759
I'll handle this.

362
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,599
Take Yang Awu to see Yang Cheng this week.

363
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,599
Why see Yang Cheng?

364
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,960
What if Yang Cheng tells him everything?

365
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,319
Do you think a kid could handle that?

366
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:44,599
Yang Cheng might not make it through the week.

367
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,119
The cancer cells are spreading too fast.

368
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,079
Alright.

369
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,799
I also want to talk to you about Lao Kang.

370
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,000
There was a slight accident.

371
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,200
But as long as his lawyer can't see him,

372
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:06,119
I can keep everything under control here.

373
00:18:06,599 --> 00:18:08,920
Why can't his defense lawyer see him?

374
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,799
The way you're handling this is very strange.

375
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:12,359
People will find out, you know.

376
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:13,920
You have your way of doing things,

377
00:18:14,319 --> 00:18:15,240
and I have mine.

378
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:16,720
It's only a few days until the pretrial conference.

379
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:21,000
I'll keep Lao Kang in the detention center.

380
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,079
Lao Kang treats Yang Awu better than anyone.

381
00:18:27,119 --> 00:18:30,400
Manipulating Xiao Sun to dismiss the jurisdictional objection...

382
00:18:30,799 --> 00:18:31,920
You did a great job.

383
00:18:32,039 --> 00:18:34,839
Clean and quiet.

384
00:18:35,039 --> 00:18:35,839
So,

385
00:18:36,759 --> 00:18:38,279
don't turn your guilt

386
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,319
into indecision.

387
00:18:42,359 --> 00:18:44,240
You're already on my boat, my friend.

388
00:18:44,839 --> 00:18:45,759
Don't get seasick.

389
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:48,960
If you do, get used to it.

390
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:08,680
Where?

391
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:10,759
Where are we going?

392
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,599
Do you want to see Grandpa?

393
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,000
Grandpa?

394
00:19:19,319 --> 00:19:20,359
Who is Grandpa?

395
00:19:20,799 --> 00:19:21,799
Quick, call Dr. Sun!

396
00:19:21,799 --> 00:19:23,240
The patient in bed three is crashing!

397
00:19:24,039 --> 00:19:26,559
Grandpa is your mom's dad.

398
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,519
I want to see Dad.

399
00:19:38,839 --> 00:19:40,039
What's wrong? What did you say?

400
00:19:41,599 --> 00:19:42,680
I want to see Dad.

401
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:44,440
Lao Kang.

402
00:19:50,319 --> 00:19:52,359
Okay, I got it.

403
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,319
Let's go.

404
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,519
Then let's go see Lao Kang.

405
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,319
Let's go see the person you want to see.

406
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:22,680
Hey, Ding Ning.

407
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,240
I have plans tonight.

408
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,880
Can you look after Awu for me?

409
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,519
Sure, but...

410
00:20:31,279 --> 00:20:31,960
The thing is...

411
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,680
I'm meeting a friend.

412
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:33,119
I'm meeting a friend.

413
00:20:38,039 --> 00:20:39,160
She's here. Gotta go.

414
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,559
Sorry I'm late.

415
00:20:44,599 --> 00:20:46,000
No worries, I'm early.

416
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,839
See what you'd like to order.

417
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,759
You look really nice today.

418
00:21:19,079 --> 00:21:22,559
Song... Songfan, what do you want to eat?

419
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:25,839
I... I'd like...

420
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,079
How about we get a combo for two?

421
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,079
Hey, Zhou Hao.

422
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:57,880
How exactly did you do it?

423
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,920
I've practically been sleeping at the station.

424
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,640
I just hope my friend

425
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,559
hasn't paid an irreversible price.

426
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,319
The bad news is,

427
00:22:06,319 --> 00:22:08,319
I'll be at least another 15 minutes.

428
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:09,400
Can you wait for me?

429
00:22:11,279 --> 00:22:11,960
There's no time.

430
00:22:13,279 --> 00:22:14,400
Let's not be late.

431
00:22:15,079 --> 00:22:16,279
Listen, I'll head in first.

432
00:22:16,279 --> 00:22:17,480
You go in when you arrive.

433
00:22:17,799 --> 00:22:18,440
It's the same thing.

434
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,480
Alright. Safety first.

435
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:22,039
Are you sure you're okay by yourself?

436
00:22:22,359 --> 00:22:23,440
Don't worry.

437
00:22:24,359 --> 00:22:25,119
See you in a bit.

438
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,599
Okay, bye.

439
00:22:34,279 --> 00:22:34,920
Hello.

440
00:22:42,079 --> 00:22:42,880
Please fill out this form.

441
00:22:50,079 --> 00:22:50,799
Number four.

442
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:51,839
Thank you.

443
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:52,920
Here's my phone.

444
00:22:53,079 --> 00:22:53,759
Okay.

445
00:23:39,039 --> 00:23:40,440
Your friend Zhao Yijie hired me

446
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,799
as your criminal defense lawyer.

447
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:42,680
My name is Zhou Hao.

448
00:23:43,079 --> 00:23:44,920
I'm exercising my legal right to meet with you.

449
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,279
Currently, this case

450
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,920
has already entered the trial phase.

451
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:56,400
Did someone hit you?

452
00:23:59,359 --> 00:24:00,799
That obviously isn't an old injury.

453
00:24:02,599 --> 00:24:03,400
Tell me the truth.

454
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,079
Is someone threatening you?

455
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,680
The visitation time isn't over yet.

456
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,200
And my questioning isn't finished.

457
00:24:17,559 --> 00:24:18,920
I didn't say I was taking him away.

458
00:24:20,079 --> 00:24:21,359
Then you should know

459
00:24:21,599 --> 00:24:22,640
our conversation

460
00:24:22,759 --> 00:24:24,640
legally shouldn't be heard by anyone else,

461
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:25,519
including you.

462
00:24:39,759 --> 00:24:41,359
How did you get these injuries?

463
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,480
Who hit you?

464
00:24:47,519 --> 00:24:49,000
He won't speak with you standing here.

465
00:24:49,119 --> 00:24:50,079
So please step out.

466
00:24:50,519 --> 00:24:51,240
No.

467
00:24:52,119 --> 00:24:54,759
He either gets into fights or hurts himself.

468
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,480
I'm trying to protect him.

469
00:24:56,759 --> 00:24:58,039
I strongly suspect

470
00:24:58,039 --> 00:25:00,319
that you caused his injuries.

471
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:02,240
The reason he won't speak

472
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:04,720
is because he's afraid you'll beat him again.

473
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:05,880
So please step out.

474
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,279
Don't move.

475
00:26:03,039 --> 00:26:03,599
Okay.

476
00:26:04,559 --> 00:26:05,200
Turn around.

477
00:26:08,759 --> 00:26:09,960
All right.

478
00:26:15,039 --> 00:26:16,200
I missed you so much, baby.

479
00:26:16,519 --> 00:26:18,160
I knew you'd be acquitted.

480
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,400
You've been through a lot.

481
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,880
The court investigated thoroughly,

482
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:23,960
and cleared my name.

483
00:26:40,559 --> 00:26:41,440
Let's go home.

484
00:26:42,119 --> 00:26:42,720
Let's go.

485
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:20,920
Sorry, I'm late.

486
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:21,880
Here's my ID.

487
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:22,920
My colleague is inside.

488
00:27:26,039 --> 00:27:27,759
This case involves organized crime.

489
00:27:27,799 --> 00:27:29,519
You need a task force pass to enter.

490
00:27:30,839 --> 00:27:32,519
My colleague is already inside.

491
00:27:32,559 --> 00:27:34,200
I'm going in to meet up with him.

492
00:27:34,359 --> 00:27:35,480
I have to play by the book.

493
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:37,559
No, it's Changyu Law Firm.

494
00:27:38,079 --> 00:27:39,720
Attorney Zhou Hao from Rujie Law Firm.

495
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:42,079
He went in around 8:20.

496
00:27:42,559 --> 00:27:44,079
I don't care who's inside,

497
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,559
you need a pass to get in.

498
00:27:46,319 --> 00:27:47,960
The thing is, my pass is inside, so...

499
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,200
Have a pass, you go in.

500
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,160
No pass, go get one.

501
00:28:02,759 --> 00:28:03,519
Excuse me,

502
00:28:03,519 --> 00:28:04,839
could you make an exception?

503
00:28:04,839 --> 00:28:06,640
Let me go in and check if my colleague is inside.

504
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:07,920
If not, I'll come right back out.

505
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,519
Is that okay?

506
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:10,039
Please don't disrupt our work.

507
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:49,000
Looks like the flight wasn't delayed today.

508
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:50,279
Well, it can't always be delayed.

509
00:28:50,359 --> 00:28:51,160
Here's yours.

510
00:28:53,319 --> 00:28:54,839
Excuse me, is Zhou Hao here?

511
00:28:55,599 --> 00:28:57,400
Honey, I'm the receptionist.

512
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:58,400
I'm not his babysitter.

513
00:28:58,400 --> 00:28:59,920
Don't ask me about everything.

514
00:29:05,319 --> 00:29:06,519
Who's that? Did we get a new hire?

515
00:29:06,519 --> 00:29:07,720
Hi, is Zhou Hao here?

516
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:10,519
Her? She's Zhou Hao's external assistant.

517
00:29:10,799 --> 00:29:11,799
She's not from our company.

518
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:13,839
He hasn't been in all day.

519
00:29:13,839 --> 00:29:15,000
I haven't seen him.

520
00:29:15,559 --> 00:29:16,279
Thanks.

521
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:20,279
Okay.

522
00:29:21,119 --> 00:29:21,960
Hand it to me after you sign it.

523
00:29:34,759 --> 00:29:36,839
Is Xiao Song still in charge of the company's surveillance?

524
00:29:39,559 --> 00:29:40,200
Okay.

525
00:29:44,559 --> 00:29:45,559
Take it easy, take it easy.

526
00:29:45,559 --> 00:29:46,920
One at a time, one at a time.

527
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:47,880
We'll sort it all out.

528
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:48,359
Here's the thing.

529
00:29:48,359 --> 00:29:48,960
Xiaojia.

530
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:50,279
Give me a second.

531
00:29:50,759 --> 00:29:52,400
Do you have Zhou Hao's parents' phone number?

532
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,680
Or his home address or something?

533
00:29:54,119 --> 00:29:54,759
Zhou Hao?

534
00:29:55,559 --> 00:29:56,359
Never mind, I'll ask my mentor.

535
00:29:56,359 --> 00:29:56,960
I'll leave you to it.

536
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:57,599
Come on, come on.

537
00:30:14,119 --> 00:30:15,160
Zhou Hao is missing.

538
00:30:15,599 --> 00:30:17,599
I've looked everywhere he might be.

539
00:30:17,599 --> 00:30:19,240
I've been calling him every ten minutes.

540
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:20,480
Can't reach him at all.

541
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,200
Then I guess

542
00:30:23,599 --> 00:30:25,799
he got taught a lesson for stepping out of line.

543
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,319
Taught a lesson for stepping out of line?

544
00:30:28,799 --> 00:30:30,079
Mentor, do you know something?

545
00:30:30,079 --> 00:30:32,279
No, no. I know just as much as you do.

546
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:34,319
It's just that I'm more familiar with

547
00:30:34,319 --> 00:30:35,799
how Rujie Law Firm operates.

548
00:30:36,559 --> 00:30:37,680
How do they operate?

549
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:39,720
Does his disappearance have anything to do with his firm?

550
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:41,359
Don't worry about Zhou Hao.

551
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:42,559
Who would dare touch him?

552
00:30:43,279 --> 00:30:44,640
You should worry about yourself.

553
00:30:44,799 --> 00:30:45,799
You've had a few days to rest.

554
00:30:46,119 --> 00:30:47,160
Are you feeling any better?

555
00:30:47,759 --> 00:30:48,599
I'm doing okay.

556
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:51,039
I'll be fine once things settle down.

557
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:53,480
Then I can get back to focusing on cases.

558
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,279
Nowadays, law school graduates

559
00:30:56,279 --> 00:30:57,279
have three options.

560
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:58,799
One is to make money.

561
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:00,680
A small law firm is fine,

562
00:31:01,119 --> 00:31:02,920
but a big one like Rujie is even better.

563
00:31:03,279 --> 00:31:04,279
The second option

564
00:31:04,559 --> 00:31:05,759
is serving the people.

565
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:08,279
Working in the justice system.

566
00:31:09,119 --> 00:31:10,000
The third option,

567
00:31:12,119 --> 00:31:12,839
for a stable life,

568
00:31:14,880 --> 00:31:15,920
is becoming a corporate lawyer.

569
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:20,640
My stepdad just came to see you about this?

570
00:31:22,079 --> 00:31:23,119
He came to see me

571
00:31:24,240 --> 00:31:26,200
because he wanted to see your work environment,

572
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,559
and to check in on you.

573
00:31:27,559 --> 00:31:29,799
And to pressure you into firing me?

574
00:31:30,240 --> 00:31:31,519
Or did he find a new job for me

575
00:31:31,519 --> 00:31:32,519
and want your advice?

576
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,200
Don't you want to ask

577
00:31:34,359 --> 00:31:35,519
what kind of job

578
00:31:35,519 --> 00:31:36,559
your parents found for you?

579
00:31:37,279 --> 00:31:39,240
Why are we talking about this?

580
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:41,880
Assistant to the Legal Director at a tech company.

581
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,920
It's very laid-back.

582
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:44,559
The pay is five times what you make here.

583
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,119
You promised me before

584
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,640
that you'd settle down.

585
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:48,799
How about

586
00:31:50,039 --> 00:31:51,480
this Wednesday at 1:30 PM,

587
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,880
you go for an interview?

588
00:31:53,799 --> 00:31:55,000
An... an interview?

589
00:31:55,559 --> 00:31:56,440
Are you kicking me out?

590
00:31:57,119 --> 00:31:58,000
Are you serious?

591
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:59,680
No, I'm not kicking you out.

592
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,000
I'd hate to see you go.

593
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:05,640
I just don't want you fighting with your family.

594
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:07,359
If you fall out with your parents,

595
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:08,559
I'd feel terrible.

596
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:10,920
I just don't understand it.

597
00:32:11,599 --> 00:32:12,359
Actually, sometimes I think

598
00:32:12,359 --> 00:32:14,440
your parents have a point.

599
00:32:15,119 --> 00:32:16,119
With your health,

600
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,759
why do you insist on being a criminal defense lawyer?

601
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:20,279
Running around in all kinds of weather,

602
00:32:20,359 --> 00:32:21,519
working so hard.

603
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,279
There's no need to be so obsessed with it.

604
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:25,319
Listen to your parents.

605
00:32:25,359 --> 00:32:27,279
Just go work as an in-house counsel.

606
00:32:27,680 --> 00:32:28,319
Wouldn't that be nice?

607
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:31,920
At least that male caregiver is free now.

608
00:32:32,039 --> 00:32:33,440
His family of three is reunited.

609
00:32:34,559 --> 00:32:35,480
You do so much,

610
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:38,160
but people might not even appreciate it.

611
00:32:38,880 --> 00:32:40,000
I just don't understand.

612
00:32:40,599 --> 00:32:42,240
Why is it that all of you know

613
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:43,680
that my reporting Yu Songfan

614
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:45,119
was perfectly justified?

615
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:46,359
That lawyers have a legal right

616
00:32:46,359 --> 00:32:47,480
to oversee judicial fairness,

617
00:32:47,480 --> 00:32:48,599
a completely normal

618
00:32:48,599 --> 00:32:50,319
and even encouraged behavior...

619
00:32:50,799 --> 00:32:52,119
But when I actually do it,

620
00:32:52,119 --> 00:32:53,440
and do what I'm supposed to do,

621
00:32:53,839 --> 00:32:54,920
instead of questioning Yu Songfan,

622
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:55,839
you all think I'm in the wrong.

623
00:32:55,839 --> 00:32:56,640
N-No, I don't.

624
00:32:58,599 --> 00:33:00,000
You're not wrong. You're right.

625
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:01,440
And I admire you for it.

626
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,480
I know you.

627
00:33:02,839 --> 00:33:04,640
Even though you were his student,

628
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:05,480
or even friends,

629
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:06,880
as long as he made a mistake,

630
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:09,000
you'd report him again if given the chance.

631
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:09,759
Am I right?

632
00:33:09,759 --> 00:33:10,400
Yes.

633
00:33:10,720 --> 00:33:12,079
Then I'm not the problem.

634
00:33:12,079 --> 00:33:13,200
The problem lies with those

635
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,279
who claim to have high EQ

636
00:33:14,279 --> 00:33:15,319
and understand the ways of the world,

637
00:33:15,319 --> 00:33:17,000
but actually can't tell right from wrong.

638
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:19,319
But can you really shut them up?

639
00:33:19,559 --> 00:33:20,039
And what if, by chance,

640
00:33:20,039 --> 00:33:21,480
they happen to be the ones paying our bills?

641
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:24,039
It's not easy to survive nowadays.

642
00:33:24,039 --> 00:33:25,920
Running a law firm is so hard.

643
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:26,880
Eight years ago,

644
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:29,039
I won a lawsuit,

645
00:33:29,039 --> 00:33:29,960
but they couldn't afford to pay me,

646
00:33:29,960 --> 00:33:31,920
so they gave me this karaoke storefront.

647
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:34,079
I couldn't even be bothered to redecorate.

648
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:35,319
I just turned it into a law firm.

649
00:33:35,519 --> 00:33:37,000
Now, the people who hire us

650
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,039
are all just neighbors.

651
00:33:38,039 --> 00:33:39,000
They're ordinary people.

652
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:39,799
They don't really understand

653
00:33:39,799 --> 00:33:41,640
the rights and obligations granted by law.

654
00:33:41,799 --> 00:33:43,680
If I were your age right now

655
00:33:43,799 --> 00:33:44,680
and had an opportunity like this,

656
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:46,000
I'd have settled for a stable life long ago.

657
00:33:49,559 --> 00:33:50,799
That's all I have to say.

658
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:53,039
Just think about it.

659
00:33:55,759 --> 00:33:56,480
I need to get back to work.

660
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:36,480
You awake?

661
00:34:40,039 --> 00:34:41,719
Didn't sleep a wink last night.

662
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,760
Did you handle the matter with Yang Awu's uncle?

663
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,239
You can trust me to get it done.

664
00:34:50,320 --> 00:34:51,559
I've already had my men

665
00:34:51,559 --> 00:34:52,519
go and teach him a lesson.

666
00:34:54,480 --> 00:34:55,280
Clear your head.

667
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:57,000
I've got some bombshell news

668
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,280
that you'll definitely find interesting.

669
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,000
Do you remember

670
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,760
when Zhou Hao flew out just to see the two of us?

671
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:06,039
Yeah, I remember.

672
00:35:06,079 --> 00:35:07,639
That discovery in Lao Kang's case

673
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:09,760
wasn't found by Zhou Hao at all.

674
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,039
Actually, I should've realized it sooner.

675
00:35:13,719 --> 00:35:15,119
Someone with the patience

676
00:35:15,159 --> 00:35:18,320
to read through boxes and boxes of case files...

677
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:19,480
how could they possibly

678
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:21,239
make one tiny discovery

679
00:35:21,239 --> 00:35:22,599
and get so impatient

680
00:35:22,719 --> 00:35:23,599
that they'd fly all the way here

681
00:35:23,599 --> 00:35:25,760
just to claim credit from the two of us?

682
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:29,000
Zhou Hao just wanted to steal the credit.

683
00:35:29,199 --> 00:35:30,559
But the person who truly

684
00:35:30,599 --> 00:35:32,760
found the loopholes in Lao Kang's case

685
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:36,039
is a female paralegal working for Zhou Hao.

686
00:35:46,440 --> 00:35:47,519
I called

687
00:35:47,639 --> 00:35:49,480
Mr. Ye in Rongshan County.

688
00:35:50,119 --> 00:35:53,960
Mr. Ye said a female lawyer delivered the money.

689
00:35:54,039 --> 00:35:55,440
A female lawyer.

690
00:35:58,920 --> 00:36:00,159
So,

691
00:36:00,559 --> 00:36:01,480
from the very beginning,

692
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:04,079
Zhou Hao outsourced this job to her.

693
00:36:06,159 --> 00:36:09,840
And now, we have another new friend who knows

694
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,800
about the loopholes in Kang's case.

695
00:36:19,840 --> 00:36:21,320
How interesting.

696
00:36:22,159 --> 00:36:23,159
You think that's interesting?

697
00:36:23,719 --> 00:36:25,239
I've got something even more interesting.

698
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:28,000
Earlier, Yu Songfan followed Fang Xia's car

699
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:28,880
to your house.

700
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:31,280
He just didn't see Yang Awu at the time.

701
00:36:31,559 --> 00:36:32,880
I took precautions, too,

702
00:36:32,880 --> 00:36:34,519
and sent someone to tail Yu Songfan.

703
00:36:34,639 --> 00:36:35,920
And it's a good thing I did.

704
00:36:36,599 --> 00:36:38,280
Do you know who my guys caught on camera

705
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:39,960
living with Yu Songfan?

706
00:37:41,679 --> 00:37:43,440
Yu Songfan, have I been too polite to you?

707
00:37:43,679 --> 00:37:45,199
Who are you to mess with me?

708
00:37:46,280 --> 00:37:47,079
What's the matter?

709
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:49,320
I warned you repeatedly

710
00:37:49,679 --> 00:37:51,119
not to let them see Lao Kang.

711
00:37:52,159 --> 00:37:53,679
Yet you arranged it behind my back.

712
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:54,760
You know damn well

713
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:56,239
that if Lao Kang gets out,

714
00:37:56,400 --> 00:37:57,679
Yang Awu is done for.

715
00:37:59,679 --> 00:38:00,440
Look here.

716
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,159
I've come to you so many times.

717
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:04,400
I just wanted to discuss Lao Kang with you.

718
00:38:04,719 --> 00:38:05,880
Lao Kang is a good man.

719
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:08,119
And he saved my grandson's life.

720
00:38:09,159 --> 00:38:10,400
I can't hurt him.

721
00:38:11,199 --> 00:38:13,519
Are you addicted to playing the good guy?

722
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,559
Fine.

723
00:38:16,320 --> 00:38:18,000
Let's forget about our deal then.

724
00:38:18,159 --> 00:38:19,880
But the case you want me to handle...

725
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:21,199
I'll get it done for you.

726
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,280
Whether Yang Awu is a hostage or not,

727
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,639
I'll still get it done for you.

728
00:38:24,639 --> 00:38:26,480
All the dirty work you want done.

729
00:38:27,239 --> 00:38:29,679
But I just can't break this child's heart.

730
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:36,000
I almost believed you.

731
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:38,760
Just for a second.

732
00:38:41,079 --> 00:38:43,480
Lao Yu, you really are clever.

733
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:44,920
I truly never expected

734
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:47,039
that you'd team up with the girl

735
00:38:47,039 --> 00:38:49,239
who ruined your career as a judge.

736
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:52,559
Are you a masochist?

737
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:56,079
Or are you looking for a spring romance?

738
00:38:56,079 --> 00:38:57,079
What did you say? Shut up!

739
00:38:57,079 --> 00:38:58,079
Did you two sleep together?

740
00:38:58,079 --> 00:38:59,400
Shut your filthy mouth!

741
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,480
You're a piece of shit.

742
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:02,400
That doesn't mean everyone is as filthy as you!

743
00:39:05,960 --> 00:39:07,239
Try me!

744
00:39:08,199 --> 00:39:09,679
Come on! Bring it!

745
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,039
Come on!

746
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:15,519
You've finally lost it, Lao Yu.
